cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this report, cite the archived report using its Zenodo DOI."
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23367498"
title: "Higher journal fees are associated with more citations, but price is not a quality score"
authors:
  - family-names: "Piamsa-nga"
    given-names: "Punpiti"
repository-code: "https://github.com/punpiti/apc-quality-report"
url: "https://punpiti.github.io/apc-quality-report/"
abstract: >-
  An English-language report with a Thai translation examining associations
  between advertised article processing charges and journal citation measures,
  OpenAlex-derived within-field quartiles, and curated journal lists.
  The analysis uses 15,176 journal records retrieved from OpenAlex on
  14 October 2026. Results describe associations and do not establish
  causal effects of price on journal quality.
keywords:
  - article processing charges
  - journals
  - OpenAlex
  - bibliometrics
  - open access
